# Feature Request: Add NVIDIA API support for Kimi K2.5 model #962

notsointresting started this conversation in Ideas

Feature Request: Add NVIDIA API support for Kimi K2.5 model #962

Jan 30, 2026 · 1 comment

Discussion options

## 

notsointresting Jan 30, 2026

### What feature would you like to see?

## Feature Request

### Description

I'd like to propose adding support for using Kimi K2.5 model via NVIDIA's
API endpoint. NVIDIA hosts the Kimi K2.5 model at `https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1`
which allows users to access the model with an NVIDIA API key instead of a
Kimi account. Reference: https://docs.api.nvidia.com/nim/reference/moonshotai-kimi-k2-5

### Proposed Solution

  * Add a new `nvidia` provider type that uses OpenAI-compatible API with
`reasoning_content` field
  * Add `kimi nvidia login/logout/status` commands for API key management
  * Store API key in `~/.kimi/.env`

### Use Case

  * Users who have NVIDIA API credits can use Kimi K2.5
  * Alternative access method for regions where Kimi direct API may have
issues
  * 40 RPM rate limit on NVIDIA's free tier

### Implementation

I have a working implementation ready if this feature is accepted.

### Additional Context

  * NVIDIA API is OpenAI-compatible
  * Supports 256K context, thinking mode, tool calling
  * Tested and working

### Additional information

